        "text": "The next unresolved question in my work revolves around verifying whether the variables `\u7d50\u679c\uff12` and `\u7d50\u679c2` refer to the same entity. To address this, I will perform a small check to determine if these variables are equivalent. Here is the step-by-step process I will follow:\n\n1. **Define the Variables**: \n   - `\u7d50\u679c1` is set to 10.\n   - Both `\u7d50\u679c\uff12` and `\u7d50\u679c2` are set to 5.\n\n2. **Print the Variables**: \n   - This will help us see if the variables hold the same value.\n\n3. **Perform the Subtraction**: \n   - Calculate `\u7d50\u679c1 - \u7ed3\u679c2` to ensure the operation works as expected.\n\nLet's write the Python code to perform these steps:\n\n```python\n# Define result1,result2, and\u7d50\u679c\uff12with specific values\n\u7d50\u679c1 = 10  # First result\n\u7d50\u679c\uff12 = 5   # Second result\n\u7d50\u679c2 = 5   # Second result (same value as\u7d50\u679c\uff12)\n\n# Print the values of the results\nprint('\u7d50\u679c1:',\u7d50\u679c1)\nprint('\u7d50\u679c\uff12:',\u7d50\u679c\uff12)\nprint('\u7d50\u679c2:',\u7d50\u679c2)\n\n# Perform subtraction\ndifference =\u7d50\u679c1 - \u7ed3\u679c2\n\n# Print The Result\nprint('Difference (\u7d50\u679c1 - \u7ed3\u679c2):', difference)\n```\n\nBy printing the values of `\u7d50\u679c\uff11`, `\u7d50\u679c\uff12`, and `\u7d50\u679c2`, we can determine if they are the same. Then, we will perform the subtraction and print the result. This will help us verify the consistency of the variables."
